WEBVTT

00:00.430 --> 00:07.030
Alright, when working with tables inside
Microsoft Word, we want to ensure that

00:07.030 --> 00:12.370
headings are semantically marked up
correctly, either row or column headings.

00:12.530 --> 00:18.310
So, first we click into the table, and a
new table design menu item shows up, and

00:18.310 --> 00:24.290
selecting that brings up this new ribbon,
and for this header row, we want to select

00:24.290 --> 00:31.290
that, meaning that that header row is real
headings. And then the first column in our

00:31.290 --> 00:35.630
case is also headings, so we're going to
select that as well. There may be an

00:35.630 --> 00:41.650
option that repeat header row on multiple
pages, if it's a long table, select that

00:41.650 --> 00:42.730
as well if you have that option.

